22	// The tests of Seed (DEVDESK-505, NX-02a, step 7; Plane DEVDESK-542):
23	//
24	//	Seed(ctx, SeedDeps{Runner, Forwarder, Copier, Clock, Store}, baseURL, p, out) (SeedResult, error)
25	//
26	// against a provisioned fake Nexus (fakenexus_test.go), the scripted kubectl of
27	// upstream_test.go, a recording port-forward, a recording image copier that models
28	// the three registries (upstream, docker-hosted, docker-proxy) and the fake clock.
29	//
30	// What the tests assume, to settle with the code (the choices are the tester's):
31	//   - Order: credentials from the store (admin, then bench-pull; nothing else is
32	//     touched when one is missing) -> the state of the upstream (ReadUpstream, read
33	//     only) -> OCI layout in a temporary folder -> port-forward to
34	//     svc/bench-upstream:5000 -> the upstream images, in the order of Dataset() ->
35	//     the port-forward is stopped -> the docker-hosted images, in the order of
36	//     Dataset() -> the PullThrough images through docker-proxy -> the two listings.
37	//   - An image is copied only when the manifest digest read at its destination
38	//     (ImageCopier.ManifestDigest) differs from the one of the data set. A
39	//     ManifestDigest error of kind SeedFailed ("manifest unknown") means "absent";
40	//     any other error stops the seed. Every Copy carries PreserveDigests.
41	//   - Credentials: no credentials for the upstream (no authentication), the stored
42	//     admin for docker-hosted, the stored bench-pull for docker-proxy. The proxy is
43	//     only ever read for a PullThrough image (F9): a read of mirror/uncached through
44	//     it would cache it. The group is never touched.
45	//   - A PullThrough image already listed by docker-proxy with the right digest is
46	//     not pulled again (the second run copies nothing). How Seed knows (a REST
47	//     listing, or a read through the proxy) is left to the code.
48	//   - NX-02a: a cut upstream is an error (kind SeedFailed, "the upstream is cut")
49	//     without any write: restoring it is NX-02b. An upstream that is missing or still
50	//     starting is a SeedFailed too, and an upstream URL that is not the bench's is
51	//     refused (it names NEXUS_BENCH_UPSTREAM_URL): the bench would push to a registry
52	//     the proxy does not read. Seed never scales, never applies, never writes to
53	//     Nexus.
54	//   - The final listings are read by REST with the admin account, after every copy.
55	//     docker-proxy must list exactly the PullThrough images, docker-hosted exactly
56	//     the hosted ones (name and tag; a digest the instance lists must be the one of
57	//     the data set). A missing component is waited for, by Clock, 30 s at most (the
58	//     same bound for both repositories, H-COMPONENTS), then it is a SeedFailed. A
59	//     component outside the data set is a SeedFailed at once, without waiting, that
60	//     names the repository and says to run `mise run nexus-bench:reset`.
61	//   - Every failure is a *BenchError; the error of the copier, of the forwarder or
62	//     of the REST client stays reachable with errors.Is/As and is never printed.
63	//     A cancelled context is returned so that errors.Is(err, context.Canceled) holds.
64	//   - The port-forward is opened once per Seed, stopped on every path, and its
65	//     address must be a loopback literal or Seed refuses it before any copy.
66	//   - The temporary folders (layout, pull-through target) are under TMPDIR and gone
67	//     when Seed returns. Output: lines that start with "seed: ", no password. A nil
68	//     writer is accepted.
69	//   - SeedResult.Images is Dataset(): every digest filled, PullThrough true exactly
70	//     for the images cached in docker-proxy (DatasetImage has no CachedInProxy field).
71	
